    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this July 4th, the lineup is anchored by two elite speed threats who carry our highest daily efficiency scores: **Corbin Carroll** (74.49) and **Brice Turang** (73.39). **Corbin Carroll** enjoys a dual advantage against Brandon Woodruff; while the SP_xERA of 3.83 is respectable, the combination of favorable park factors and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery profile creates a massive stolen base floor. Similarly, **Brice Turang** benefits from a soft matchup against Meibrys Viloria\u2019s battery mate, with a 5.47 xERA opponent and a projected #3 hole giving him the prime real estate needed to rack up counting stats. **Josh Naylor** (71.12) rounds out our top-tier plays, as he should feast on Bieber\u2019s 5.52 xERA; the significant SP skill boost outweighs his slight park penalty, making him a cornerstone for RBI production today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (48.88), who fell just shy of the threshold despite a strong projection due to the #1 order slot. Ultimately, we opted for the higher floor offered by **Zach McKinstry** (50.89) and **Alex Freeland** (50.84), as their specific matchup variables against Wandy Peralta and Cal Quantrill marginally edged out the overall efficiency profile of **Travis Bazzana**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Kyle Karros** (63.92), whose high score is buoyed by a significant 14% park boost and a strong #2 lineup spot, though he must contend with an elite 1.88s pop-time catcher which slightly dampens his aggressive base-running upside.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational risks as the day progresses. The primary concern remains the official confirmation for **Brice Turang**; while we have penciled him into the #3 spot, any shift lower in the order will necessitate a quick recalibration of his efficiency score. Additionally, despite his elite 0.418 xwOBA, **James Wood** faces a stern test against Beau Ashcraft (3.19 xERA); while his raw talent provides a 52.66 score, the presence of an elite 1.89s catcher behind the plate creates a volatility risk for his stolen base contributions. Elsewhere on the depth chart, we continue to monitor the progress of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Tyler Soderstrom** on the IL, as their absence remains a significant drag on our overall offensive flexibility.",
